# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. `cargo build` regenerates all of it, and target/ on the
# development machine is well over a gigabyte - firmware does not belong in
# history. Publish images as Release assets pinned to a tag instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
**/target/
*.hex
*.uf2
*.elf
*.bin
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Gazell archive IS intentionally committed, under vendor/gzll/ : the build
# needs that one file and nothing else from the nRF5 SDK, and Nordic's licence
# permits redistributing the binary when license.txt travels with it. There is
# deliberately no rule touching vendor/ - excluding it would make a fresh clone
# unbuildable, and re-including a file whose parent directory is excluded is not
# something git can do.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local archives that are NOT part of the project: superseded firmware, SDK
# copies kept for forensics, quarantined experiments from a refactor.
/reference/
/_quarantine-*/
/_tmp-*/

# Python scratch caches from tools/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Logs written by the build and comparison scripts.
*.log
build.log
objcopy.log

# PCAP captures from the RF-link investigation.
*.pcap

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
